  "interpretation": [
    "LFQ protein: normalized log2 within-pair differences {'P905_906': -0.5038, 'P907_908': -0.5511, 'P909_910': -0.5076, 'P941_942': -0.5016} (mean -0.516, SD 0.0235); 4 of 4 pairs negative and nearly identical, so the residual SD is tiny; the trend prior (lower at high abundance) then moderates it less towards a larger variance and it passes q < 0.05.",
    "Normalization does not create the LFQ decrease: raw log2 differences {'P905_906': -0.6182, 'P907_908': -0.8548, 'P909_910': -0.6917, 'P941_942': -0.6963} (mean -0.7153); the median-normalization offsets add {'P905_906': 0.1144, 'P907_908': 0.3038, 'P909_910': 0.1841, 'P941_942': 0.1947} per pair (raloxifene runs scaled up), shrinking the effect and making it more uniform across pairs.",
    "LFQ peptide evidence (FlashLFQ peptide table): DFSPSGIFGAFQR[+0.0]: mean within-pair normalized log2 difference -0.048 (per pair {'P905_906': -0.1601, 'P907_908': -0.2126, 'P909_910': 0.2701, 'P941_942': -0.0896}; detection types {'MSMS': 8}); LGELPSWILMR[+0.0]: mean within-pair normalized log2 difference None (per pair {'P905_906': None, 'P907_908': None, 'P909_910': None, 'P941_942': None}; detection types {'MSMSAmbiguousPeakfinding': 6, 'MSMS': 2}); LGELPSWILMR[+15.9949]: mean within-pair normalized log2 difference -0.6567 (per pair {'P905_906': -0.8456, 'P907_908': -0.6469, 'P909_910': -0.8166, 'P941_942': -0.3178}; detection types {'MSMS': 8}).",
    "Spectral counts are small: protein PSMs per run {'AZ905': 6, 'AZ907': 6, 'AZ909': 6, 'AZ906': 12, 'AZ908': 13, 'AZ910': 12, 'AZ941': 7, 'AZ942': 7} (mean 8.62); within-pair log2 PSM ratios {'P905_906': 1.0, 'P907_908': 1.1155, 'P909_910': 1.0, 'P941_942': 0.0}. Poisson noise alone gives a per-pair log2-ratio SD of about 0.72.",
